    "description": "The Fulfillment Console reads and edits order lines from the legacy relational database. OrderSearchService currently embeds SELECT statements, OrderEntryService repeats INSERT statements, and OrderAdjustmentService contains UPDATE and DELETE statements for the same table. Each component knows placeholder syntax, column order, and date conversion rules. A schema change to the order_lines table therefore requires searching the entire repository, and the DBA cannot identify all statements that require tuning. Introduce one OrderLinesData component that owns every SQL operation for that table. Its methods accept and return simple record structures, while callers receive formatted rows or edited records. Keep transaction control in the services, keep formatting in the presentation layer, and prohibit direct table access from controllers and domain rules. Include read, insert, update, and delete operations in the component, with a small integration test that proves no SQL remains elsewhere.",
    "decision_statement": "Should all SQL for each database table be confined to one component whose methods exchange plain record structures, rather than leaving statements in transaction scripts?",
    "notes": "table-data-gateway fits the single OrderLinesData component owning all SQL for the table behind record structures; row-data-gateway and data-access-object are the per-row and store-abstraction alternatives, with dao-factory supporting creation."
  },
